<section class="block" aria-labelledby="h-install">
  <p class="label">install</p>
  <h2 class="display" id="h-install">Start with one command.</h2>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Node.js 24 or later is all it needs. <strong>No account, no configuration,</strong> and it never calls a language model or a remote service.</p>
      <p>Run <code>npx openteleport</code> for the guided transfer wizard. Keep it on your PATH with <code>npm install --global openteleport</code>, or run it with npx.</p>
      <p class="links"><a href="https://github.com/Open-Teleport/openteleport">github.com/Open-Teleport/openteleport</a><br /><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/openteleport">npmjs.com/package/openteleport</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="term big"><pre><span class="cmd">$ npx openteleport --help</span>

  move      read an agent from one app, write it into another
  export    save an agent as a .jetpack file
  import    write a .jetpack file, or an agent folder, into an app
  list      the agents an app has
  inspect   what a .jetpack file or an agent folder holds
  validate  check a bundle against the format and scan it for secrets
  adapters  the supported apps, and whether each is installed here</pre></div>
  </div>
</section>

